BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-18-andrzej-wereszczynski@ceico.cz
DTSTAMP:20261128T040319Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Prague:20261118T113000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Prague:20261118T123000
SUMMARY:Cosmo: Andrzej Wereszczyński – Standard Model Effective Field Th
 eory and Oscillons (and vortices)
LOCATION:A. Kochanovské Hall
DESCRIPTION:Andrzej Wereszczyński (Jagiellonian University\, Kraków\, Pol
 and)\n\nStandard Model Effective Field Theory and Oscillons (and vortices)
 \n\nI will show that the inclusion of a dimension-six operator in the Higg
 s potential has a dramatic impact on the stability of oscillons in the SU 
 (2) bosonic sector of the Standard Model\, extending their lifetime by mor
 e than an order of magnitude. This happens for the physical value of the r
 atio between the Higgs and W boson masses\, m_H /m_W =1.556 and for the di
 mension-six operator O_6 = (Φ†Φ)^3 whose coupling constant is below th
 e current upper bound. I will also show how this operator changes the form
 ation of vortices\, which form the ground state of EW theory at a large ex
 ternal magnetic field.\n\nhttps://www.ceico.cz/seminars/archive/2026/#2026
 -11-18-andrzej-wereszczynski
URL:https://www.ceico.cz/seminars/archive/2026/#2026-11-18-andrzej-wereszcz
 ynski
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-25-duarte-feiteira@ceico.cz
DTSTAMP:20261128T040319Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Prague:20261125T113000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Prague:20261125T123000
SUMMARY:Cosmo: Duarte Feiteira – Cosmological gravitational particle prod
 uction and implications for dark matter phenomenology
LOCATION:Institute of Plasma Physics building - room 421
DESCRIPTION:Duarte Feiteira (University of Helsinki\, Finland)\n\nCosmologi
 cal gravitational particle production and implications for dark matter phe
 nomenology\n\nParticle production in the Early Universe is one of the corn
 erstones of modern cosmology and plays an important role in dark matter ph
 enomenology. In this talk\, I will first discuss the gravitational product
 ion of scalars during inflation. I will compare Bogolyubov coefficient and
  Starobinsky stochastic approaches\, showing that they only agree in the l
 imit of infinitely long inflation. High-scale inflation is very efficient 
 in particle production\, leading to constraints on the existence of free\,
  light\, and stable scalars: such particles are viable only if their masse
 s are below the eV scale or if the reheating temperature is in the GeV ran
 ge. These constraints motivate scenarios in which dark matter is produced 
 via low-temperature freeze-in. In this framework\, I will consider warm Hi
 ggs portal dark matter. In scenarios where the Standard Model thermal bath
  never reached high temperatures\, dark matter production can be suppresse
 d. This allows for a significant dark matter-Higgs coupling\, enabling war
 m dark matter detection via Higgs decay at colliders. I will further discu
 ss the strong Lyman-α bound on the dark matter mass\, excluding masses be
 low 50-100 keV\, and show how the shape of the warm dark matter momentum d
 istribution is highly non-thermal and not captured by the commonly used α
 βγ-parametrization.\n\nhttps://www.ceico.cz/seminars/archive/2026/#2026-
 11-25-duarte-feiteira
URL:https://www.ceico.cz/seminars/archive/2026/#2026-11-25-duarte-feiteira
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-27-ilka-brunner@ceico.cz
DTSTAMP:20261128T040319Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Prague:20261127T110000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Prague:20261127T120000
SUMMARY:Strings: Ilka Brunner – Towards Quantum elliptic cohomology
LOCATION:Room 226
DESCRIPTION:Ilka Brunner (Arnold Sommerfeld Center for Theoretical Physics\
 , LMU München\, Germany)\n\nTowards Quantum elliptic cohomology\n\nI will
  discuss how N=1 gauge theories on a disk times a torus suggests the exist
 ence of a quantum deformation of equivariant elliptic cohomology. We give 
 a geometric interpretation of potential anomalies\, and discuss Ward ident
 ities.\n\nhttps://www.ceico.cz/seminars/archive/2026/#2026-11-27-ilka-brun
 ner
URL:https://www.ceico.cz/seminars/archive/2026/#2026-11-27-ilka-brunner
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2026-11-30-lorenzo-grimaldi@ceico.cz
DTSTAMP:20261128T040319Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Prague:20261130T140000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Prague:20261130T150000
SUMMARY:Strings: Lorenzo Grimaldi – One-loop self-energy of Type II heavy
  string states
LOCATION:Room 226
DESCRIPTION:Lorenzo Grimaldi (Tor Vergata University of Rome\, Italy)\n\nOn
 e-loop self-energy of Type II heavy string states\n\nThe free string spect
 rum is highly degenerate\, with a degeneracy that grows exponentially with
  the mass\, making highly excited strings natural candidates for black-hol
 e microstates in the string/black-hole correspondence. A non-vanishing str
 ing coupling $g_s$ makes massive states unstable and shifts their masses\,
  partially lifting this degeneracy. At one loop\, the imaginary part of th
 e self-energy gives the tree-level width for the decay into two lower-mass
  states\, whereas the real part gives the mass shift and is generally IR-d
 ivergent. We firstly focus on the states of maximal spin at each level in 
 the NS-NS sector of Type II theories\, for which the analysis simplifies b
 ecause they cannot mix with other states. Exploiting elliptic functions\, 
 we obtain a closed-form expression for the worldsheet integral on the toru
 s. We then regularize and renormalize the remaining modular integral via t
 he $i\\varepsilon$-prescription\, extracting mass shifts and decay widths 
 up to level $N=10$.\n\nhttps://www.ceico.cz/seminars/archive/2026/#2026-11
 -30-lorenzo-grimaldi
URL:https://www.ceico.cz/seminars/archive/2026/#2026-11-30-lorenzo-grimaldi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-11-antonio-antunes@ceico.cz
DTSTAMP:20261128T040319Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Prague:20270111T140000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Prague:20270111T150000
SUMMARY:Strings: António Antunes – Towards the explicit construction of 
 generic 2d CFTs
LOCATION:Room 226
DESCRIPTION:António Antunes (LPENS\, Paris\, France)\n\nTowards the explic
 it construction of generic 2d CFTs\n\nOur understanding of interacting CFT
 s in d>2 dimensions was revolutionized by modern developments in the analy
 tical and numerical conformal bootstrap. The poster child of this program\
 , the non-exactly solvable 3d Ising CFT\, is now understood to an unpreced
 ented level of detail. In contrast\, our understanding of 2d CFTs encompas
 ses large classes of exactly solvable models (the so-called rational CFTs)
 \, and a set of universal bootstrap results which apply only to "generic" 
 non-exactly solvable CFTs of which no concrete example is available. In th
 is talk\, we summarize our recent attempts at constructing such theories b
 y coupling exactly solvable CFTs and flowing to IR fixed points. We will d
 iscuss perturbative and non-perturbative constructions as well as some dua
 l bounds on the set of conserved currents in the IR..\n\nhttps://www.ceico
 .cz/seminars/archive/2027/#2027-01-11-antonio-antunes
